  "dynamic": true,
  "editorial_revision": 2,
  "reference_text": "In 1930 Gandhi proposed breaking the Salt Laws to begin a mass civil disobedience movement. Salt tax affected the poorest people. He announced a march from his ashram in Ahmedabad to Dandi on the Arabian Sea. Picking up salt at Dandi was an act of defiance of the Salt Laws and a signal for others to defy the law. This connected an everyday material with non-violent political action. No numerical crowd size, automatic tax repeal, boiling demonstration or immediate independence is asserted.",
